a) Each branch splits into $Y$ and $N$ at the next question.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A0) at (2.1,2);
\draw (O)--(A0) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\coordinate (A1) at (2.1,-2);
\draw (O)--(A1) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\coordinate (B0) at (4.2,3);
\draw (A0)--(B0) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\coordinate (B1) at (4.2,1);
\draw (A0)--(B1) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\coordinate (B2) at (4.2,-1);
\draw (A1)--(B2) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\coordinate (B3) at (4.2,-3);
\draw (A1)--(B3) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\coordinate (C0) at (6.3,3.5);
\draw (B0)--(C0) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\node[right] at (C0) {$YYY$};
\coordinate (C1) at (6.3,2.5);
\draw (B0)--(C1) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\node[right] at (C1) {$YYN$};
\coordinate (C2) at (6.3,1.5);
\draw (B1)--(C2) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\node[right] at (C2) {$YNY$};
\coordinate (C3) at (6.3,0.5);
\draw (B1)--(C3) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\node[right] at (C3) {$YNN$};
\coordinate (C4) at (6.3,-0.5);
\draw (B2)--(C4) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\node[right] at (C4) {$NYY$};
\coordinate (C5) at (6.3,-1.5);
\draw (B2)--(C5) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\node[right] at (C5) {$NYN$};
\coordinate (C6) at (6.3,-2.5);
\draw (B3)--(C6) node[midway,above] {$Y$};
\node[right] at (C6) {$NNY$};
\coordinate (C7) at (6.3,-3.5);
\draw (B3)--(C7) node[midway,below] {$N$};
\node[right] at (C7) {$NNN$};
\node at (1.05,4.3) {Question 1};
\node at (3.15,4.3) {Question 2};
\node at (5.25,4.3) {Question 3};
\node[anchor=west] at (6.3,4.3) {Outcome};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The outcomes are $YYY$, $YYN$, $YNY$, $YNN$, $NYY$, $NYN$, $NNY$ and $NNN$.
b) There are $8$ complete paths.
Number of outcomes:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}2 \times 2 \times 2\\&=8\end{aligned}$

Draw three first-stage branches, labelled $B$, $A$ and $T$.
After $B$ is drawn, only $A$ and $T$ remain.
After $A$ is drawn, only $B$ and $T$ remain.
After $T$ is drawn, only $B$ and $A$ remain.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (F1) at (2.2,1.8);
\coordinate (F2) at (2.2,0);
\coordinate (F3) at (2.2,-1.8);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,1.2);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,0.6);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-0.6);
\coordinate (E5) at (4.8,-1.2);
\coordinate (E6) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O)--(F1) node[midway,above] {$B$};
\draw (O)--(F2) node[midway,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$A$};
\draw (O)--(F3) node[midway,below] {$T$};
\draw (F1)--(E1) node[midway,above] {$A$};
\draw (F1)--(E2) node[midway,below] {$T$};
\draw (F2)--(E3) node[midway,above] {$B$};
\draw (F2)--(E4) node[midway,below] {$T$};
\draw (F3)--(E5) node[midway,above] {$B$};
\draw (F3)--(E6) node[midway,below] {$A$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$(B,A)$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$(B,T)$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$(A,B)$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$(A,T)$};
\node[right] at (E5) {$(T,B)$};
\node[right] at (E6) {$(T,A)$};
\node at (1.1,3.2) {Draw $1$};
\node at (3.5,3.2) {Draw $2$};
\node[anchor=west] at (4.8,3.2) {Outcome};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The outcomes are $(B,A)$, $(B,T)$, $(A,B)$, $(A,T)$, $(T,B)$ and $(T,A)$.
